    "Pages you have already read that are still in memory beyond the preload range, counted back from the current page without a gap. They stay until the “Page images kept in memory” limit is reached, so anything from zero to dozens is normal." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pages you have already read that are still in memory beyond the preload range, counted back from the current page without a gap. They stay until the “Page images kept in memory” limit is reached, so anything from zero to dozens is normal."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "先読みの範囲より外側に、現在のページから途切れずにメモリへ残っている既読ページ数です。読み終えたページは環境設定「メモリに残しておくページ画像」の上限に達するまで残るので、この数がゼロでも数十でも正常です。"
